Date:   Sun Oct 18 20:25:13 2026 +0200

    fix: keep the dictation on the clipboard after a sent paste and close the review gaps in delivery
    
    - Never put the old clipboard back after a sent paste: nothing proves the target took
      Ctrl+V, and one that stalls would paste the old clipboard. The focus read, the settle
      delay and the second window query leave the delivery path with it.
    - A cancel before the keystroke restores the old clipboard only when it still holds
      exactly our text and the snapshot is complete and worth restoring.
    - The keystroke port re-checks the abort signal and "Useful Voice is in front" at the
      moment it writes, after any wait in the queue; the one-shot fallback does the same and
      is killed when the signal aborts.
    - The PowerShell host handles an EPIPE on stdin like a death, starts a request's clock
      when it is written, and rejects an aborted request while it still waits.
    - Esc is global only while recording again.
    - Delivery timeout recomputed with the one-shot rerun, hotkey repeat window 600 ms, the
      language picker reads the current foreground window, the "dictating into" lookup is
      tied to a service sequence that every start and cancel changes, unused
      ownProcessName removed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

