     1	# Useful Voice — agent notes
     2	
     3	Cross-platform dictation app. macOS: Swift (`Sources/UsefulVoiceCore`,
     4	`Sources/UsefulVoiceApp`). Windows: Electron + TypeScript (`windows/`, whose
     5	`src/core` mirrors the Swift core). Transcription: Deepgram Nova-3 via
     6	`POST /v1/listen`.
     7	
     8	## Verification gates
     9	
    10	- macOS: `make test` (Swift Testing suite) and `swift build`
    11	- Windows: `cd windows && npm run verify` (typecheck + vitest + build +
    12	  Electron self-test)
    13	- Packaging smoke: `cd windows && npx electron-builder --win --dir`
    14	- Windows E2E: `cd windows && env -u ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE npm run e2e` (Playwright drives the
    15	  built app with `--e2e --uv-data-dir=<scratch>`: hidden windows, fixture data, no tray or
    16	  global hotkeys). `E2E_OUT=<dir>` moves the HTML report, traces, videos and screenshots
    17	  (default `windows/e2e-results/`). CI runs it on `windows-latest` and uploads the report.
    18	  The video needs Playwright's ffmpeg (`npx playwright install ffmpeg`); without it Playwright never
    19	  resumes the windows and they hang blank, with no error.
    20	- Windows first run (`components/firstRun.ts`, gate in `core/firstRun/gate.ts`): `--force-first-run` shows it and
    21	  saves nothing (settings.json and data.json frozen for the whole process); `--first-run-step=<welcome|engine|errKey|deepgramKey|microphone|errMic|tryIt|tryItDone|done>`
    22	  jumps to a step with sample data. Under `--e2e` only, `main/e2eStub.ts` fakes Deepgram (a key starting `valid` works,
    23	  `offline` fails like a dead network, anything else is a 401) and Chromium's fake microphone is on. E2E fixtures seed
    24	  `firstRunCompleted: true` unless a spec asks otherwise (`e2e/first-run.spec.ts`).
    25	- Windows dictation E2E (`e2e/dictation.spec.ts`, `e2e/hud-a11y.spec.ts`, helpers in `e2e/harness.ts`): real recordings from the
    26	  fake microphone through the e2e stub. Under `--e2e` main exposes `globalThis.__uv` (`index.ts`) and `globalThis.__uvTray.menu()`
    27	  (`tray.ts`, the menu the tray would show, since no icon is created). Chromium's fake microphone beeps all the time, so a
    28	  silence-limit spec swaps the recorder window's `getUserMedia` for a scripted tone (`useScriptedMicrophone`). The shortest
    29	  limits the app allows are 15 s of silence and 30 s of recording, so those two specs take 20 s and 35 s. Never press the
    30	  hotkey to completion in a spec: it would paste into whatever is in front of the machine.
    31	
    32	## Delivery
    33	
    34	A hotkey dictation pastes wherever the cursor is when the text is ready, on both platforms; only Useful Voice's own
    35	window in front at delivery (a stop from the dock) copies instead, unless the dictation started there. On Windows the
    36	paste, the foreground read and the sound cues go through one long-lived PowerShell (`src/main/powershellHost.ts`,
    37	started at app ready, types compiled once); the delivery order lives in `src/core/delivery/pasteFlow.ts` and the
    38	clipboard rule in `src/core/delivery/clipboardRestore.ts` (a sent Ctrl+V counts as delivered and the dictation stays on
    39	the clipboard; the old clipboard is put back only when a cancel arrives before the keystroke and nothing newer was copied).
    40	
    41	## Windows renderer layout
    42	
    43	`windows/src/renderer/`: `renderer.ts` (entry) wires `shell.ts` (rail, header, banners,
    44	navigation with `navigate(page, anchor?)`) to `pages/{stream,notes,vocabulary,insights,settings}.ts`;
    45	shared pieces live in `components/` and styles in `styles/` (`tokens.css` with the
    46	`[data-theme]` light and dark blocks, `components.css`, `components/*.css`, `pages/*.css`; the
    47	build concatenates every file in that order). `hud.ts` draws the HUD and floating language
    48	picker windows. `--preview-features` shows controls whose backend has not shipped
    49	(`components/flags.ts`).
    50	
    51	## `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` gotcha
    52	
    53	Agent shells (Claude Code, Codex) may export `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1`. With it set,
    54	`electron` runs as plain Node and `import 'electron'` resolves to the empty
    55	`electron:electron` pseudo-module — the self-test then dies before app code
    56	with either a `cjsPreparseModuleExports` TypeError or
    57	`SyntaxError: ... does not provide an export named 'app'`. Neither is an app
    58	or Electron defect. Run Electron commands with the sentinel unset:
    59	
