   180	---
   181	
   182	## Keyboard and tray
   183	
   184	- **Hotkey**: default `Control+Alt+Space`, changeable in Settings. Press to start,
   185	  press again to stop. If another app already owns the combination the app tells
   186	  you, instead of silently never starting.
   187	- **Tray icon**: filled while recording. Left-click opens the window. The menu
   188	  offers start/stop, cancel, retry, copy-last and the pages.
   189	- **Closing the window does not quit.** The app is tray-resident so the hotkey keeps
   190	  working. Quit from the tray menu.
   191	
   192	## Data and privacy
   193	
   194	Everything lives in `%APPDATA%\Useful Voice`:
   195	
   196	| File | Contents |
   197	| --- | --- |
   198	| `settings.json` | preferences; the API key inside is DPAPI-encrypted |
   199	| `data.json` | dictionary, corrections, shortcuts, history, notes |
   200	| `diagnostics.log` | recent problems: never transcript text, never the key |
   201	
   202	Audio is held in memory only while transcribing and is never written to disk. Each
   203	recording's audio is uploaded to Deepgram for transcription, along with your
   204	dictionary's correct spellings as keyterms. Nothing else leaves your PC, and there
   205	is no analytics or tracking. Uninstalling keeps this folder on purpose; Settings
   206	shows the path so you can remove it yourself.
   207	
   208	## Known gaps
   209	
   210	- **Not code-signed.** SmartScreen will warn until a certificate is configured.
   211	- **Geist is not bundled.** The UI asks for Geist and falls back to Segoe UI, the
   212	  same allowance the macOS build makes with SF Pro. Bundling the font files would
   213	  remove the difference.
   214	- **Paste confirmation is indirect.** Ctrl+V never clears the clipboard, so the app
   215	  cannot see whether the target took the text: it reports "pasted" when the keystroke
   216	  went out, and leaves the dictation on the clipboard so a second Ctrl+V works.
   217	  Reading the target's text needs a UI-automation dependency, which was avoided so the
   218	  app ships no native module.

